    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-075 correction + ADR-076 proposed.** Direct CSS analysis of Wikipedia's 220 KB Vector 2022 stylesheets **disproved** ADR-075's \"missing sticky support\" hypothesis, and documented the real measured cascade gaps.\n\n## What the CSS analysis found\n\nFetched both `load.php?modules=...&only=styles&skin=vector-2022` stylesheets (220 KB combined), then counted feature usage:\n\n| Feature | Count | Where used |\n|---|---|---|\n| `var(--)` | **569** | Colors, spacing, breakpoints |\n| `@media` | **91** | Mixed forms — `all and (min-width:640px)`, `screen and (max-width:639px)`, `prefers-color-scheme`, `prefers-reduced-motion` |\n| `@supports` | **75** | Progressive enhancement gates |\n| `:where(` | 16 | Low-specificity wrappers |\n| `:has(` | 8 | Parent selectors |\n| `position: sticky` | **2** | Both `.vector-sticky-pinned-container` (TOC only) |\n\n**Header elements (`mw-navigation`, `p-navigation`, `vector-main-menu`) have NO sticky declarations.** They're correctly `pos=static`. ADR-075's theory was wrong.\n\n## ADR-076 proposal\n\nFour ordered sub-tasks:\n\n1. **076-A: `@media` prefixed forms** (highest impact, ~60-100 lines). ADR-027's parser likely doesn't handle `all and (min-width:...)` or `screen and (max-width:...)` prefixes. If those fail to parse, mobile-only rules apply at desktop width — matching the observed anomalies (`p-navigation` laid out at 984px with `w=0`, `mw-navigation` with `h=0`).\n2. **076-B: CSS custom properties** (569 uses, one-to-two sessions).\n3. **076-C: `@supports` evaluation** (~50 lines).\n4. **076-D: `:where()` / `:has()`** (deferred).\n\nVerification: after 076-A, re-run Wikipedia at 984px and check whether `p-navigation` / `vector-main-menu` become `display: none` (per Firefox). Then check `<h2>History` position.\n\n## What this PR does NOT do\n\n- **Does not fix anything.** ADR-076 is Proposed. Implementation is next session's work.\n- **Does not remove ADR-075's traces.** `pos=` and `ABS_PUSH` traces stay in place — they enabled the disproval.\n- **Does not change any production code.**\n\n## Diagnostic lesson recorded\n\nADR-073's permanent-trace policy enabled both hypotheses and disprovals this session. The trace infrastructure was correct; only one interpretation was wrong. That's the intended pattern: measure → hypothesize → verify → correct. Hypothesis proposed and disproved in the same session is a feature, not a bug.\n\n## Test count\n\n694 / 2646 unchanged (docs-only PR).\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Diagnostic correction.** No code change. Two ADRs updated/added.\n\nRefs #283\n",
